This aircraft is a JSBSim model of Bitcraze's Crazyflie 2.1 Brushless nano quadrotor in the configuration of
the IDSIA nano-drone system-identification benchmark, written by PteroLabs in 2026, with meshes converted from
the Crazyflow simulator's cf21B model.

The flight model (crazyflie_bl.xml, the files it assembles, Engines/ and initGrnd.xml) is PteroLabs' work,
distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0; see LICENSE in this folder for its text. Its numbers
come from:

  Busetto et al., "Nonlinear System Identification Nano-drone Benchmark", arXiv:2512.14450 (2025): the
  vehicle's configuration and mass, and the flight data of its training flights (chirp, random, square) on
  which the thrust, climb-loss, rotor-drag, motor, rotor-inertia, body-inertia and CG-trim values were
  identified.
    https://arxiv.org/abs/2512.14450
    https://github.com/idsia-robotics/nanodrone-sysid-benchmark

  Bitcraze crazyflie-firmware (GPL-3.0), commit 9912584c85db92dbbba14334ffed20ebabba463e: the arm length
  (ARM_LENGTH) and the thrust-to-torque ratio (THRUST2TORQUE) in
  src/platform/interface/platform_defaults_cf21bl.h, the motor numbering in
  src/modules/src/power_distribution_quadrotor.c.
    https://github.com/bitcraze/crazyflie-firmware

  Bitcraze's Crazyflie 2.1 Brushless datasheet and product pages: the frame, the 55-35 propeller, the
  08028-10000KV motor's data quoted for comparison, and which propeller turns which way on which motor.
    https://www.bitcraze.io/documentation/hardware/crazyflie_2_1_brushless/crazyflie_2_1_brushless-datasheet.pdf

  Crazyflow (learnsyslab/crazyflow, MIT), commit c95f69bc54f830e859fee4ac5734bf571acd81f3: the meshes
  (meshes/NOTICE) and their placement in crazyflow/drones/cf21B_500.xml, on which the propeller-hub and foot
  heights were measured; its inertia and rotor-inertia values are quoted for comparison.
    https://github.com/learnsyslab/crazyflow

Chosen, with no source, and marked so where they appear: the CG height (the circuit-board plane), the feet's
spring, damping and friction, the meshes' roughness, the chase camera.

Crazyflie is a trademark of Bitcraze AB. The name says which vehicle this models; Bitcraze does not endorse
PteroSim, and this model is not a Bitcraze product.
